00:43:06.385 --> 00:43:08.465
So the way this organization

00:43:08.465 --> 00:43:09.745
is structured

00:43:09.950 --> 00:43:13.070
is that the directors of the organization

00:43:13.630 --> 00:43:14.430
are

00:43:14.830 --> 00:43:16.830
individuals

00:43:17.150 --> 00:43:22.510
within the town governments of the seven towns that are on the Hop River Trail.

00:43:23.025 --> 00:43:26.625
There are two town managers slash town administrators.

00:43:26.785 --> 00:43:28.625
There's a public works director,

00:43:28.785 --> 00:43:31.105
a director of planning and development,

00:43:31.665 --> 00:43:34.465
actually two directors of planning and development,

00:43:34.800 --> 00:43:36.720
the parks and recs director,

00:43:37.040 --> 00:43:39.920
and one town engineer that sit on the panel.

00:43:41.360 --> 00:43:44.080
And then there's a series of officers

00:43:44.240 --> 00:43:46.000
that do the actual work.

00:43:46.320 --> 00:43:48.000
So, board of directors

00:43:48.495 --> 00:43:50.735
is, has the authority

00:43:51.215 --> 00:43:53.455
in the power to authorize

00:43:53.455 --> 00:43:54.095
things.

00:43:55.135 --> 00:43:55.695
They

00:43:56.255 --> 00:43:59.775
essentially have another group of people that do the actual labor.

00:44:00.575 --> 00:44:06.100
So, it's a structure that's modeled after a bunch of the other trail associations,

00:44:06.580 --> 00:44:11.380
because it keeps the deciding power within the towns themselves

00:44:14.515 --> 00:44:18.755
to look at what direction the Trail Association is going to do.

00:44:19.235 --> 00:44:22.035
