A pure electric vehicle is going to have a bigger battery than a plug in hybrid

03:08:30.585 --> 03:08:31.146
and

03:08:32.024 --> 03:08:44.905
you know you're going to want to look at electric vehicles with hundreds of miles of range on the battery, not tens of miles like a hybrid. The point of a hybrid is that if I remember the statistics, something like 85%

03:08:45.145 --> 03:08:45.705
of

03:08:46.210 --> 03:08:53.730
car use in this country is less than 50 miles a day. So you can do the vast majority statistically,

03:08:53.890 --> 03:08:58.930
you know, if you are an average person on just battery. Now a municipal application

03:08:59.295 --> 03:09:06.255
is going to be something different. You're going to have to look at the specifics vehicle to vehicle and I think a reasoned approach

03:09:06.255 --> 03:09:17.590
to getting an electric vehicle or a hybrid would take a look at how we've been using this over the past several years, what the average trips are, how many trips per day, the distances and things like that.

